    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0491" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3419</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Group</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Department acknowledges the
                    receipt of your letter of May 18, 1921, with reference to the decision of the
                    American Group approving the proposed formation of a council to consider
                    Consortium matters.</p>
                <p>The Department would like to know whether this proposal has met the approval of
                    all of the Groups. It is noted that in the telegram from Mr. Lamont to you of
                    May 14,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d321-f1"/> transmitted to you by the Department on
                    May 17, 1921,<anchor n="59" xml:id="d321-f2"/> the matter was to be submitted to
                    the Japanese Group representative in London.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. M.
                            Dearing</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d321-f1" n="58" xml:id="d321-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 332, May 14, from the Ambassador in France, <ref target="#pg365"
                        >p. 365</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d321-f2" n="59" xml:id="d321-f2-content">
                <p>Letter of May 17 not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
